      "writtenOn": "2026-06-10T13:50:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For ICO, I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary. A reader from new_reader will always be created with metadata_loaded set to false.\nThe reader should always be fresh and the call should be safe to repeat in the Rust early-return.\n\nIncomplete input shouldn\u0027t be an issue after it has passed through MakeFromIcoStream because it either succeeds or fails, it doesn\u0027t come back later for incomplete scenarios.",
