      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, can we avoid all these copies if we force everything into SkData upfront, and then slice/subset as needed?  Something like this\n\n```\n    sk_sp\u003cSkData\u003e data \u003d stream-\u003egetData();\n    if (!data) {\n        data \u003d SkStreamPriv::CopyStreamToData(stream.get());\n        ...\n    }\n    SkMemoryStream dataStream(data);\n    ...\n    ...\n\n    auto entryData \u003d data-\u003eshareSubset(offset, size);\n    auto entryStream \u003d std::make_unique\u003cSkMemoryStream\u003e(entryData);\n```",
